Task 1: Configure Circuit Breakers for Services
Subtask 1.1: Deploy Sample Microservices
First, let's deploy a simple microservices application that we'll use to demonstrate circuit breaker functionality.

Step 1: Create the Application Namespace
kubectl create namespace circuit-breaker-demo
kubectl label namespace circuit-breaker-demo istio-injection=enabled
Step 2: Deploy the Frontend Service
Create the frontend service configuration:

cat <<EOF > frontend-service.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: frontend
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: frontend
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: frontend
        version: v1
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: frontend
        image: kennethreitz/httpbin
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: frontend
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  selector:
    app: frontend
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    name: http
EOF
Apply the configuration:

kubectl apply -f frontend-service.yaml
Step 3: Deploy the Backend Service
Create the backend service that we'll apply circuit breaker policies to:

cat <<EOF > backend-service.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: backend
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backend
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: backend
        version: v1
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: backend
        image: kennethreitz/httpbin
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        env:
        - name: DELAY_RESPONSE
          value: "false"
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: backend
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  selector:
    app: backend
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    name: http
EOF
Apply the backend configuration:

kubectl apply -f backend-service.yaml
Step 4: Verify Service Deployment
Check that all services are running:

kubectl get pods -n circuit-breaker-demo
kubectl get services -n circuit-breaker-demo
Wait until all pods show Running status before proceeding.

Subtask 1.2: Create Circuit Breaker Destination Rule
Now we'll configure the circuit breaker policy using Istio's DestinationRule.

Step 1: Create Basic Circuit Breaker Configuration
cat <<EOF > circuit-breaker-destinationrule.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: DestinationRule
metadata:
  name: backend-circuit-breaker
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  host: backend.circuit-breaker-demo.svc.cluster.local
  trafficPolicy:
    outlierDetection:
      consecutiveGatewayErrors: 3
      consecutive5xxErrors: 3
      interval: 30s
      baseEjectionTime: 30s
      maxEjectionPercent: 50
      minHealthPercent: 50
    connectionPool:
      tcp:
        maxConnections: 10
      http:
        http1MaxPendingRequests: 5
        http2MaxRequests: 10
        maxRequestsPerConnection: 2
        maxRetries: 3
        consecutiveGatewayErrors: 3
        h2UpgradePolicy: UPGRADE
EOF
Step 2: Apply the Circuit Breaker Configuration
kubectl apply -f circuit-breaker-destinationrule.yaml
Step 3: Verify the Configuration
kubectl get destinationrule -n circuit-breaker-demo
kubectl describe destinationrule backend-circuit-breaker -n circuit-breaker-demo
Subtask 1.3: Configure Virtual Service for Traffic Routing
Create a Virtual Service to route traffic to our backend service:

cat <<EOF > backend-virtualservice.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: backend-vs
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  hosts:
  - backend.circuit-breaker-demo.svc.cluster.local
  http:
  - match:
    - uri:
        prefix: "/"
    route:
    - destination:
        host: backend.circuit-breaker-demo.svc.cluster.local
        port:
          number: 80
    timeout: 10s
    retries:
      attempts: 3
      perTryTimeout: 3s
EOF
Apply the Virtual Service:

kubectl apply -f backend-virtualservice.yaml
Task 2: Simulate Failures and Monitor Circuit Breaker Actions
Subtask 2.1: Set Up Monitoring and Observability
Step 1: Deploy a Test Client Pod
Create a test client to generate traffic:

cat <<EOF > test-client.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: test-client
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
