Subtask 3.2: Create Optimized Circuit Breaker Configuration
Based on the test results, let's create a more finely-tuned configuration:

Step 1: Create Enhanced Circuit Breaker Configuration
cat <<EOF > optimized-circuit-breaker.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: DestinationRule
metadata:
  name: backend-circuit-breaker-optimized
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  host: backend.circuit-breaker-demo.svc.cluster.local
  trafficPolicy:
    outlierDetection:
      # Reduce consecutive errors for faster detection
      consecutiveGatewayErrors: 2
      consecutive5xxErrors: 2
      # Check more frequently
      interval: 10s
      # Shorter ejection time for faster recovery
      baseEjectionTime: 15s
      # Allow higher ejection percentage
      maxEjectionPercent: 75
      # Require at least one healthy instance
      minHealthPercent: 25
      # Split window for better detection
      splitExternalLocalOriginErrors: true
    connectionPool:
      tcp:
        # Increase max connections for higher throughput
        maxConnections: 20
        # Add connection timeout
        connectTimeout: 5s
      http:
        # Increase pending requests
        http1MaxPendingRequests: 10
        # Increase concurrent requests
        http2MaxRequests: 20
        # Allow more requests per connection
        maxRequestsPerConnection: 5
        # Reduce retries to fail faster
        maxRetries: 2
        # Add request timeout
        h2UpgradePolicy: UPGRADE
        # Enable keep-alive
        useClientProtocol: true
EOF
Step 2: Apply the Optimized Configuration
First, remove the old configuration:

kubectl delete destinationrule backend-circuit-breaker -n circuit-breaker-demo
Apply the new configuration:

kubectl apply -f optimized-circuit-breaker.yaml
