Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Circuit Breaker Not Activating
Symptoms: Requests continue to succeed even when errors are expected

Solutions:

# Check if Istio injection is enabled
kubectl get namespace circuit-breaker-demo --show-labels

# Verify DestinationRule is applied correctly
kubectl get destinationrule -n circuit-breaker-demo -o yaml

# Check Envoy configuration
kubectl exec -n circuit-breaker-demo $BACKEND_POD -c istio-proxy -- curl -s localhost:15000/config_dump | grep circuit_breaker
Issue 2: All Requests Failing
Symptoms: All requests return 503 status codes

Solutions:

# Check if all instances are ejected
kubectl exec -n circuit-breaker-demo $BACKEND_POD -c istio-proxy -- curl -s localhost:15000/stats | grep outlier_detection.ejections_active

# Reduce maxEjectionPercent or increase minHealthPercent
# Wait for baseEjectionTime to pass for recovery
Issue 3: Inconsistent Behavior
Symptoms: Circuit breaker behavior varies between requests

Solutions:

# Check if multiple DestinationRules exist
kubectl get destinationrule -n circuit-breaker-demo

# Verify service mesh configuration
istioctl proxy-config cluster test-client.circuit-breaker-demo
Monitoring and Observability
Setting Up Prometheus Metrics
Create a ServiceMonitor for circuit breaker metrics:

cat <<EOF > circuit-breaker-monitoring.yaml
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: circuit-breaker-metrics
  namespace: circuit-breaker-demo
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backend
  endpoints:
  - port: http-monitoring
    interval: 15s
    path: /stats/prometheus
EOF
Key Metrics to Monitor
Important circuit breaker metrics to track:

envoy_cluster_outlier_detection_ejections_active: Number of currently ejected hosts
envoy_cluster_upstream_rq_pending: Number of pending requests
envoy_cluster_upstream_rq_retry: Number of retried requests
envoy_cluster_upstream_rq_timeout: Number of timed-out requests
envoy_http_downstream_rq_xx: HTTP response code distributions
Best Practices and Recommendations
Circuit Breaker Configuration Guidelines
Start Conservative: Begin with higher thresholds and gradually tighten them
Monitor Closely: Always monitor the impact of circuit breaker changes
Test Thoroughly: Use load testing to validate configuration changes
Consider Service Criticality: Critical services need different thresholds
Plan for Recovery: Ensure baseEjectionTime allows for proper recovery
